        "triedShellInClaude": true,
        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed all three issues in `collapsible.tsx:122` by turning the clickable header `<div>` into a native `<button type=\"button\">`. I couldn't re-run the linter because there's no Biome or Ultracite setup in this directory, so the fix isn't verified yet.\n\n**Why this works:** all three rules flag a click handler on an element that isn't interactive. A `<button>` is interactive, so the rules stop applying. It can also be reached with Tab and pressed with Enter or Space without any extra key handlers. I didn't add `role=\"button\"` plus `tabIndex` plus `onKeyDown` to the `<div>`, because Ultracite's `useSemanticElements` rule would likely flag that and ask for a `<button>` anyway.\n\n**Behavior is unchanged:**\n- `onClick={openTrigger}`, `className`, and the flex layout stay the same.\n- I added style resets so the header looks the same as before: no background or border, no padding or margin, inherited `font`, `color` and `textAlign`, and `width: \"100%\"`. The full width is needed because buttons otherwise shrink to fit their content, unlike a `<div>`.\n- `type=\"button\"` stops it from submitting a form if it's ever placed inside one.\n\n**One addition:** I added `aria-expanded={open}`, so screen readers announce whether the section is open or closed.\n\n**Needs your decision:** the caller in `Stats/index.tsx` passes `label={<h3>…</h3>}`, so there's now a heading inside a button. HTML doesn't allow that, and screen readers will read the heading as plain button text, so it won't appear in heading navigation. The usual fix is to put the button inside the heading (`<h3><button>…</button></h3>`). That means changing the caller, which is outside the one file I was allowed to edit.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "**Behavior is unchanged:** - `onClick={openTrigger}`, `className`, and the flex layout stay the same. - I added style resets so the header looks the same as before: no background or border, no padding or margin, inherited `font`, `color` and `textAlign`, and `width: \"100%\"`."
        ],
        "behaviourMentions": [
          "**Behavior is unchanged:** - `onClick={openTrigger}`, `className`, and the flex layout stay the same. - I added style resets so the header looks the same as before: no background or border, no padding or margin, inherited `font`, `color` and `textAlign`, and `width: \"100%\"`."
